1. ACCURACY WITHIN STRATUM -- never pooled, and here is why 
------------------------------------------------------------------------------ 
200 cases: E-easy-rule-correct=68  H-hard-rule-failed=45  M-maybe-random=87
 
stratum (n)            light                        deep-                        deep+ 
  E-easy-rule-co (68)   59/68  =  86.8% (95% CI 76.7-92.9)   63/68  =  92.6% (95% CI 83.9-96.8)   63/68  =  92.6% (95% CI 83.9-96.8) 
  H-hard-rule-fa (45)   34/45  =  75.6% (95% CI 61.3-85.8)   41/45  =  91.1% (95% CI 79.3-96.5)   39/45  =  86.7% (95% CI 73.8-93.7) 
  M-maybe-random (87)   72/87  =  82.8% (95% CI 73.5-89.3)   85/87  =  97.7% (95% CI 92.0-99.4)   79/87  =  90.8% (95% CI 82.9-95.3) 

The E stratum is cases a geographic rule already got right, so every arm 
should score high there and it carries little information. H is the rule's 
failures and M a broader MAYBE draw: those are where the arms separate. 
A single pooled accuracy over these three would be an artefact of the mix. 

