2. THE PAIRED TESTS -- valid pooled, and this is the power 
------------------------------------------------------------------------------ 
calibration set alone, 200 cases 
  model   light -> deep-      25 gained,   1 lost,  26 discordant, p = 0.0000 
  search  deep- -> deep+       0 gained,   8 lost,   8 discordant, p = 0.0078 
  total   light -> deep+      23 gained,   7 lost,  30 discordant, p = 0.0052 

pooled with the experiment's 27 scorable cases = 227 paired cases 
  model   light -> deep-      29 gained,   3 lost,  32 discordant, p = 0.0000 
  search  deep- -> deep+       1 gained,   8 lost,   9 discordant, p = 0.0391 
  total   light -> deep+      27 gained,   8 lost,  35 discordant, p = 0.0019 

what the sample can now resolve 
  model   32 discordant pairs -> SIGNIFICANT at 0.05 (p = 0.0000) -- the second arm is better 
  search  9 discordant pairs -> SIGNIFICANT at 0.05 (p = 0.0391) -- THE SECOND ARM IS WORSE 
  total   35 discordant pairs -> SIGNIFICANT at 0.05 (p = 0.0019) -- the second arm is better 

  minimum detectable split at 0.05, given the discordant pairs observed: 
    model   n=32  needs 23 of 32 one way (observed 29 gained / 3 lost) 
    search  n=9   needs 8 of 9 one way (observed 1 gained / 8 lost) 
    total   n=35  needs 24 of 35 one way (observed 27 gained / 8 lost) 

