3. DOES CONFIDENCE STILL ORDER ACCURACY? -- the routing policy's premise 
------------------------------------------------------------------------------ 
The cascade rests on the light arm's own confidence separating its right 
answers from its wrong ones. At n=27 that was high 12/12, medium 10/11, 
low 0/4 -- four cases deciding the escalation tier. Re-tested here.
 
light  Haiku, packet 
  high    98/98  = 100.0% (95% CI 96.2-100.0) 
  medium  60/74  =  81.1% (95% CI 70.7-88.4) 
  low      7/28  =  25.0% (95% CI 12.7-43.4) 
deep-  Opus, packet 
  high   136/136 = 100.0% (95% CI 97.3-100.0) 
  medium  47/54  =  87.0% (95% CI 75.6-93.6) 
  low      6/10  =  60.0% (95% CI 31.3-83.2) 
deep+  Opus + search 
  high   162/166 =  97.6% (95% CI 94.0-99.1) 
  medium  18/28  =  64.3% (95% CI 45.8-79.3) 
  low      1/6   =  16.7% (95% CI 3.0-56.4) 

light arm by evidence class 
  QUOTE   62/65  =  95.4% (95% CI 87.3-98.4) 
  NTEE    16/16  = 100.0% (95% CI 80.6-100.0) 
  INFER   57/87  =  65.5% (95% CI 55.1-74.7) 
  NONE    30/32  =  93.8% (95% CI 79.9-98.3) 

high+medium vs low, Fisher exact: p = 0.00000  -- confidence DOES separate right from wrong 

